      "writtenOn": "2020-06-26T17:17:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we really need deterministic ECDSA or can just use any random for sign?  RFC 6979 is planned to be approved by NIST in SP 800 186-5, which is draft, but current requirements is that k should be random and different messages shouldn\u0027t be signed with same k. I\u0027m going to replace it later to cr50-wide DRBG to comply with this requirement. Hope this won\u0027t break expectations somewhere.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 458,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "2cee525d3fecb6efec00de8bdf8d761c6afe19d1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a33c484e_7b18a30f",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 458,
